# Grid table with combined row- and column-spanning

Two tables. The first has a single cell spanning two rows AND two columns
(the case most implementations get wrong; note the unbroken bottom border —
the corner rule omits the internal corner beneath the merged cell). The
second arranges an independent rowspan next to a colspan.

## A 2x2 merged cell

+-------+-------+-------+
| A 2x2         | B     |
+...............+-------+
|               | C     |
+---------------+-------+

## A rowspan next to a colspan

+-------+-------+-------+
| R     | S spans       |
+.......+-------+-------+
|       | C     | D     |
+-------+-------+-------+
